09366893768, -1.8411625623703003, -0.4661625623703003, -16.546098709106445, -0.35859906673431396, -17.13252067565918, -0.41377049684524536, -17.68414878845215, -0.5513359308242798, -13.570608139038086, -0.44560855627059937, -0.2143016904592514, -13.621603965759277, -0.05910353362560272, -11.498623847961426, -0.18612419068813324, -10.55785846710205, -0.43285879492759705, -7.042491912841797, -0.042491741478443146, -0.21379932761192322, -0.017515970394015312, -3.9810502529144287, -0.7310503125190735, -3.533045768737793, -0.15804579854011536, -9.291336059570312, -0.29133591055870056, -12.726691246032715, -0.25794097781181335, -10.394969940185547, -1.3949694633483887, -12.47730827331543, -1.0710585117340088, -5.475111961364746, -0.7251117825508118, -0.4844453036785126, -10.774227142333984, -0.08672703057527542, -10.58747673034668, -0.1499767005443573, -4.24426794052124, -0.3692677915096283, -6.914242267608643, -0.35174205899238586, -13.260482788085938, -0.7604829668998718, -1.7573087215423584, -0.8823087215423584, -10.95222282409668, -0.13972315192222595, -19.093753814697266, -0.8554725646972656, -3.1398026943206787, -0.7023026347160339, -14.663856506347656, -1.507606029510498, -0.5893598794937134], "math": "**Step 1: Multiply**\n173 × 29 = 173 × 20 + 173 × 9 = 3460 + 1557 = 5017\n\n**Step 2: Subtract**\n5017 − 451 = 4566\n\nANSWER: 4566", "code": "## The function\n\n```python\ndef split_kv(pages, k):\n    \"\"\"Split `pages` into k contiguous chunks, preserving order.\n\n    Chunk sizes differ by at most one (the remainder is spread over the\n    earliest chunks). If k > len(pages), each element gets its own chunk.\n    \"\"\"\n    if k <= 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"k must be a positive integer\")\n\n    n = len(pages)\n    if n == 0:\n        return []\n\n    k = min(k, n)                 # can't have more chunks than items\n    base, extra = divmod(n, k)    # e.g. 10 items, 3 chunks -> base=3, extra=1\n\n    chunks = []\n    start = 0\n    for i in range(k):\n        size = base + (1 if i < extra else 0)\n        chunks.append(pages[start:start + size])\n        start += size\n    return chunks\n```\n\n## Example\n\n```python\npages = list(range(1, 11))          # 10 \"pages\"\nchunks = split_kv(pages, 3)\n\nfor i, chunk in enumerate(chunks, 1):\n    print", "zh": "**分页 KV cache（PagedAttention，vLLM 提出）**：它把每条序列的 K/V 张量按固定粒度（如每 16 个 token 一块）切成若干\"页块\"，所有页块统一存放在一块连续显存池里，再用一个块表（block table）记录\"逻辑位置 → 物理块\"的映射，思路直接借鉴操作系统的虚拟内存分页。\n\n**为什么省显存**：传统实现要为每条请求预留 `max_seq_len` 长度的连续 KV 空间，实际生成往往远短于此，这些\"预留但没用\"的空洞就是内部碎片；而分页只按真实 token 数分配块，块大小固定且可复用，浪费基本只剩最后一个不满的块和极小的块表开销。\n\n**额外收益**：由于块可被多个请求共享，前缀缓存、并行采样/beam search 的写时复制（copy-on-write）几乎零成本地实现，配合块级换入换出还能支持抢占式调度，从而在同样显存下跑更大的 batch 和更长的上下文。"}